OL,3,GNEWSA'Significant flooding' prompts
OL,4,Afire crew call outs
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 50 properties have flooded in
OL,7,FBirmingham, after heavy rain pummelled
OL,8,Fthe West Midlands.
OL,10,FThe Environment Agency (EA) issued a
OL,11,Fflood warning for Birmingham on
OL,12,FWednesday night, with fire crews called
OL,13,Fto "significant flooding" in Perry Barr
OL,14,Faround Curbar Road, Thornbridge Avenue
OL,15,Fand Haddon Road, telling people to
OL,16,Favoid the area.
OL,18,FBirmingham City Council said 55
OL,19,Fproperties in the city had experienced
OL,20,Finternal flooding, with water levels
OL,21,Freaching up to one metre in the
OL,22,Fworst-affected homes.
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
